Expose the KGSL memory-entry queue attributes for scoped CPU-placement
experiments, preserving reclaim/concurrency and default CPU/nice policy.
The already exposed general KGSL queue needs no change. Keep the implicitly
ordered devfreq queue untouched: applying attributes would clear its ordering
flag. This patch does not select a placement policy.

--- a/drivers/gpu/msm/kgsl.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/msm/kgsl.c
@@ -5390,7 +5390,7 @@
 		WQ_UNBOUND | WQ_MEM_RECLAIM | WQ_SYSFS, 0);
 
 	kgsl_driver.mem_workqueue = alloc_workqueue("kgsl-mementry",
-		WQ_UNBOUND | WQ_MEM_RECLAIM, 0);
+		WQ_UNBOUND | WQ_MEM_RECLAIM | WQ_SYSFS, 0);
 
 	INIT_WORK(&kgsl_driver.mem_work, _flush_mem_workqueue);
 
